{-
   Specialization that does not terminate - milestone 6, waypoint G2.

   # resolver: ownership

   A file of its own for the phase-order reason `Reject.Call.yana` gives one level up, taken one step
   further: which specializations a program needs is discovered by the reachability walk, which runs
   after the bodies and only where nothing has reported - so a file with any other diagnostic in it
   could never reach this one.
-}

data Boxed(a) {value: a}

-- Polymorphic recursion: each round is called at a type built from the last, so there is no fixed
-- set of instantiations for a worklist over argument lists to run out of. Nothing about the program
-- is infinite - it is *specialization* that cannot represent it, which is why the message is about
-- the choice of lowering rather than about the program, and why the erased ABI is the answer that
-- compiles it.
fn grow(->x: a) -> I32 = grow(Boxed {value: x})

fn main() -> I32 = grow(1)
